{
 "_readme": [
  "Phase R level data (addendum 4 section 6). One entry per level 1-30; the generator (prototype/placement.gd) reads these knobs.",
  "Levels 1-6 are hand-set from the addendum table; 7-30 are interpolated and rough on purpose.",
  "hazard_rate: bar | half_bar | beat - how often hazards act. plate_coverage: fraction of a bar's 36 tiles that may be plates.",
  "plate_patterns: allowed patterns (row, block are level-1 material; checker/column_wave/spiral are beat-rate patterns).",
  "gate_opening / sweeper_gap: widths in world units (a tile is 2). types_per_bar: hazard types that may share a bar",
  "(level 1 starts at 1 and reaches types_per_bar_final in wave 5). orbiter_pairs: opposite-spin pair allowed",
  "(level 1: only from orbiter_pairs_from_wave). orbiter_period: bar | half_bar (the fast variant, levels 4+).",
  "lives: 0 = no lives (level 1), 3 from level 2. density_curve: multiplier per wave on hazards per bar.",
  "song_tempo: 1.0 | 1.05 | 1.10 - which time-stretched mp3 plays (_105, _110); the ONE beatmap's times are divided by it in BeatClock. Brief 2b: 1.0 level 1, 1.05 level 2, 1.10 from level 3.",
  "player_speed: the player's speed as a multiple of the scroll speed. 2.2 on levels 1-2, 2.3 from level 3 (brief 2b, 2026-09-20). Below ~2.1 the fairness validator cannot find fair layouts on levels 3+.",
  "song_offset_s: playback starts this far into the track (8 s level 1, 10 s later levels); written for tempo 1.0, divided by song_tempo at load.",
  "demo_bars: true = every new type/pattern gets a demo bar; false from level 7 (everything mixed).",
  "structure: curriculum = level 1's fixed wave order (addendum 3 section 3); mixed = types mix from the start."
 ],
